<title>DENMARK: Maersk, DFDS merge travel units.</title>
<headline>Maersk, DFDS merge travel units.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish travel bureaux Maersk Travel and DFDS Travel said on Friday they were merging to form Maersk DFDS Travel I/S effective January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>They said the new organisation, dealing with both business and holiday travel, would be jointly owned by Maersk Air, a unit of the A.P. Moeller shipping and oil group and DFDS, a subsidiary of shipbuilding and shipping group J.Lauritzen A/S.</p>
<p>They said in a statement that the new travel bureau would have an estimated annual turnover of one billion crowns with offices in Denmark, Britain, Norway and Sweden.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
